Introduce Docker

Get the packages required for installation.
//*
sudo snap remove curl
sudo apt install curl

//*
$ sudo apt update
//*
$ sudo apt -y install apt-transport-https ca-certificates curl software-properties-common

Add Docker official GPG key.
Run the following command and OKmake sure it shows up.

//*
$ curl -fsSL https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu/gpg | sudo apt-key add -

OKIf you get an error instead gpg: no valid OpenPGP data found.of , add it manually by running the following command:

//** if it is NOT
$ curl -O -fsSL https://download.docker.com/linux/debian/gpg
//**
$ sudo apt-key add gpg

Install Docker-CE.
//*
$ sudo add-apt-repository "deb [arch=amd64] https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu focal stable"
//*
$ sudo apt update
//*
$ sudo apt -y install docker-ce

Install Docker-Compose.
//*
$ sudo -E curl -L "https://github.com/docker/compose/releases/download/1.29.2/docker-compose-$(uname -s)-$(uname -m)" -o /usr/bin/docker-compose

Grant execute permission to the executable binary.

//*
$ sudo chmod +x /usr/bin/docker-compose

Check the version of Docker-Compose and confirm that v1.29.2 is output.

//*
$ docker-compose -v
---> docker-compose version 1.29.2, build 5becea4c

Start Docker service.

//*
$ sudo service docker start

When the Docker service has finished starting, the following message will be displayed.


